---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CliReferenceShell from '../../../components/CliReferenceShell.astro';
import css from '../../../_mock/learning-hub.css?raw';
import lessonCss from '../../../_mock/cli-lesson.css?raw';
import js from '../../../_mock/learning-hub.js?raw';
import main from '../../../_mock/studio-lesson-56-declare-project-triggers.main.html?raw';
import { lessonJsonLd } from '../../../data/lesson-jsonld.js';
const article = { headline: "Declare project triggers in triggers.yaml", description: "Declare cron, interval, file and marker triggers in triggers.yaml, then list, validate and fire them with hdrctl trigger. Tested with Hydra ETL 0.22.", datePublished: '2026-11-23', dateModified: '2026-11-23', author: 'Bechir Bejaoui' };
const jsonld = lessonJsonLd({
  path: '/cli/guides/declare-project-triggers/',
  name: article.headline,
  steps: ["Write triggers.yaml", "List the triggers", "Validate the file", "Fire one trigger by hand", "Read the history", "Break the file on purpose"],
  faq: [["What is a trigger in Hydra ETL?", "A trigger is an entry in triggers.yaml, at the project root, that says when to run the project: at a time, every so often, when a file shows up, and so on. Each trigger has a name and a type."], ["Which trigger types exist?", "The Hydra ETL 0.22 source lists seven: cron, interval, file, marker, source_change, webhook and after_project. We tested cron, interval, file and marker; the others have their own lessons."], ["Who runs the triggers?", "According to the help of hdrctl trigger, they run inside hdrctl watch and hdrctl serve. We did not leave either running in this lesson. hdrctl trigger fire NAME runs one trigger right away, and that is what we tested."], ["How do I check triggers.yaml before using it?", "Run hdrctl trigger validate. It reports unknown keys, keys that do not suit the trigger type, impossible cron expressions and workflows that do not exist. A valid file answers Triggers valid, with the number of triggers."], ["Where do I see what a trigger started?", "Run hdrctl trigger history. It reads .hydra/triggers/history.jsonl in the project and prints one line per run, with the trigger name, how it started (manual for fire) and the duration."]],
  crumbs: [['Get started', '/get-started'], ['Hydra CLI', '/cli/'], ['Guides', '/cli/guides/'], ["Triggers", '/cli/guides/declare-project-triggers/']],
});
---

<BaseLayout title="Declare project triggers in triggers.yaml" exactTitle="Hydra Triggers: triggers.yaml and hdrctl trigger | Hydra ETL" description="Declare cron, interval, file and marker triggers in triggers.yaml, then list, validate and fire them with hdrctl trigger. Tested with Hydra ETL 0.22." article={article} jsonld={jsonld}>
  <style is:global set:html={css}></style>
  <style is:global set:html={lessonCss}></style>
  <CliReferenceShell current="trigger" guide="declare-project-triggers">
    <article class="cli-article cli-guide">
      <Fragment set:html={main} />
    </article>
  </CliReferenceShell>
  <script is:inline set:html={js}></script>
</BaseLayout>

